#: ../../../src/usage/kv_cache.rst:62
msgid "Why Concatenating Is Slow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/kv_cache.rst:64
msgid "Concatenation has two costs: copying data and preventing buffer reuse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/kv_cache.rst:66
msgid ""
":func:`concatenate` creates a new array and copies the existing cache at "
"every step. Appending ``n`` positions therefore copies on the order of "
"``n^2`` elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/kv_cache.rst:70
msgid ""
"Growing the cache also prevents buffer reuse. MLX pools freed device "
"buffers, but reuses a buffer only for a similarly sized request. It does not "
"split a larger buffer for a smaller request or combine smaller buffers for a "
"larger one. Because a growing cache has a new size at every step, each "
"allocation typically comes from the driver while freed buffers remain unused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/kv_cache.rst:76
msgid ""
"This allocation work occurs on the CPU. In profiles, it appears as GPU idle "
"time between kernels rather than as a slow kernel, which can make the model "
"appear to be the bottleneck."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/kv_cache.rst:80
msgid ""
"Preallocation avoids both costs. The cache shape remains fixed, eliminating "
"both repeated copies and per-step allocations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/kv_cache.rst:84
msgid "Choosing a Chunk Size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/kv_cache.rst:86
msgid "Use a chunk size that is a multiple of 256."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/kv_cache.rst:88
msgid ""
"This both amortizes growth and enables the fused cuDNN attention kernel on "
"CUDA. For single-token attention, the key and value arrays must be slices of "
"a contiguous cache with a capacity that is a multiple of 256, and at least "
"256 positions must be in use. Other chunk sizes silently use a slower path."
msgstr ""
